Following renovations, the <a href="https://www.apple.com/retail/appleparkvisitorcenter/">Apple Park Visitor Center</a> in Cupertino, California no longer features a 3D augmented reality model of the Apple Park campus.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/07/Apple-Park-Visitor-Center.jpeg" alt="" width="1920" height="1075" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1057078" /><br/>
The area that housed the 3D model, which was called the Exhibition Space, now has wall-mounted shelves known as "Avenues" and new, rounder tables for product displays.<br/>
<br/>
The remodeling process <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/22/apple-park-visitor-center-update-in-progress/">began in July</a> and was completed recently.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><em><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Apple-Park-Visitor-Center-New-Tables.jpg" alt="" width="1440" height="810" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066819" />Apple Park Visitor Center's former Exhibition Space now displays products (<a href="http://xhslink.com/o/7QsufIrFGCB">source</a>)</em></div><br/>
The redesigned product tables have been set up at select other stores, <a href="https://x.com/ParkerOrtolani/status/2102077154729115676">such as Apple Williamsburg</a> and Apple The Mall at Bay Plaza in New York City.<br/>
<br/>
The 3D model of Apple Park had been a fixture of the Visitor Center <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2017/11/apple-park-visitor-center-opens-to-the-public/">since it opened in 2017</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Apple-Park-Visitor-Center-3D-Model.jpeg" alt="" width="1142" height="770" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066827" /><br/>
Apple Park Visitor Center functions as both a store and a tourist attraction. While the Exhibition Space is now permanently closed, visitors can still grab a coffee at the on-site Caffè Macs, purchase Apple merchandise, head up to the rooftop for a scenic view, or stroll through the adjacent "Mirage" public art installation.<br/>
